        "problem": "If $A$ is a $6\\times 8$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
        "worked_solution": "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince $A$ has $8$ columns and $3$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n8-3=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=5.$",
